## Discussion notes to carry in (2026-06-16)

1. **Submission strategy is the keystone — sequence everything off it.**
   Target venue(s) fix format, length budget, what must be undeferred,
   and the deadline to retroplan from. It also sets the arXiv tripwire
   (see [[0665]]).
2. **Name the paper portfolio explicitly before building trackers.**
   At least three latent papers, sharing the reference dataset:
   - Paper A — methods / benchmark (tracker [[0464]]).
   - Data paper — the 177-plant reference superset ([[0517]], blocked by
     0498 per-plant reconciliation).
   - Paper B — information fusion / deterministic swarm ([[0516]]).
   The data paper and methods paper share the reference, so order
   matters (data paper first as the dataset's citable home, which the
   methods paper then cites?). Fix: how many papers, the unit of each,
   and the dependency edges — THEN create the two trackers.
3. **Undeferring is a triage, not a list-reopen.** Sort the deferred
   backlog (post-arXiv experiments 0654–0662 per tracker 0644; methods
   0201/0464; next-paper material [[0564]]) into three bins — *this
   article / next article / dropped* — against the chosen venue's scope.
4. **arXiv: deferred with a tripwire** (recorded on [[0665]]) — article
   ~2 months out; post one canonical arXiv record (the article), but if
   the article slips past ~mid-August, post this report to arXiv then.
5. **MASTERPLAN has no dissemination/publications layer** — it describes
   the benchmark phases only. This session grows one, so the portfolio
   and submission timeline live in the durable plan, not just trackers.

